From 4387547afa440865566dfa961707e650fbfb17f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:33:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.9.4: six owner items - posture completeness, state-aware
 controls, honest counters

Six backlog items, all owner-reported or found on his metal, plus regression
markers pinning each one so a later change cannot silently drop it.

FIREWALL STATUS NOW REPORTS FORWARDS AND SERVICE INTERCEPTS (P2)
The posture page counted rules/objects/groups/services/zones/policies and
stopped - the nat store, which holds BOTH port forwards and Service Intercepts,
had no counter, so two live enforcement surfaces were invisible. New
fw_nat_mode_counts() splits the store by record mode. Mode is POSITIONAL FIELD 8
and an absent field is a pre-Service-Intercept record meaning "forward"
(mirrors rc's parse; unknown modes are dropped by the loader and counted as
neither - fail closed both places). The nat list is resolved LAST and consumed
immediately: reaper_fw_list_get() returns a static the next call frees. Two new
status rows (RFW_276/277).

SMART CONNECT: NO MORE DEAD SWITCH, NO MORE DEAD POINTER (P2)
Post-migration (SDN MAINFH profiles own the main network) the classic toggle
set smart_connect_x/selif and fired a bare restart_wireless - the per-band
profiles came back unchanged and nothing visibly happened. Rewriting sdn_rl
from a classic page is deliberately NOT attempted (mis-serializing it takes
down every SSID; the SDN app owns that write). Instead the page detects the
migrated state from sdn_rl itself and the button becomes a pointer to the
Network page, where the control actually lives; the "- -" cell hint and the
top banner (which sent users to a Wireless > General selector that no longer
exists there post-migration) are state-aware now too. Un-migrated boxes keep
the working classic toggle.

RAIL CLOCK RE-SYNCS (P3)
Both copies of the nav clock seeded once from <% uptime(); %> and extrapolated
forever - on a board with no RTC, where every boot and NTP correction is a
step (a ~4 h jump was observed mid-syslog on metal), a shell tab left open
across one showed the wrong time until reloaded. The twin inline scripts
collapse into js/reaper_clock.js: 1 s local tick, re-sync every 5 min and on
visibilitychange from Reaper_SecBanner.asp's new data-now attribute (a fetch
the banner loader already makes on every admin page - no new endpoint, no new
page, no langcheck surface). Corrections under 2 s are ignored, larger snap;
any failure leaves the clock ticking on its current base. Dict tokens stay in
the .asp seeds - the shared file is deliberately token-free, since the token
pass is unproven for js/ subdirectory files.

DEVICES EXPORT CARRIES RESERVATIONS (P3, owner format decision 2026-08-30)
An inventory that blanks the addresses an operator assigned was the wrong
answer, but a reservation must never export as a live lease: 'ip' keeps
meaning "has this address right now"; new reserved_ip + state columns
(reserved / reserved-out-of-pool / orphan / duplicate) qualify the claim in
all three formats. A broken pin exports as flagged, not as fact.

QOS DROPS-INTERPRETATION NOTE (P3, owner wording direction)
RQOS_124 under the class-table explainer: counters are cumulative since the
last QoS restart and normally grow only under saturation such as a speed test;
climbing while idle, or while a class sits below its ceiling, is the sign of a
real problem. Encodes the metal-validated rule of 2026-08-30 (Default
441->1191 across two speed tests, frozen at idle - predicted and confirmed).

DIAG VIF ssid_len OFF-BY-ONE (P3) - REAPER-DIAG v1.3.10
`nvram get | wc -c` counted the trailing newline, so every VIF line read +1
(live report: 7 for a 6-char SSID, 33 for the 32-hex onboarding BSS) while the
primary-radio path was exact. tr -d newline first. The pinned marker moves to
v1.3.10 in the SAME change, in both the engine's verify_markers.txt and the
lean build-scripts copy - the v2.9.3 first build failed verify on exactly that
pairing, and the lean copy turned out to still be at v1.3.8.

REGRESSION MARKERS (owner ask: fixes must not silently rebreak)
Six new verify_markers rules pin: rqos_dropnote, the nicpt status row, the
reserved_ip export column, the clock helper's visibilitychange re-sync, the
banner's data-now carrier, and the Smart Connect scWhereHint swap. Engine and
lean copies both updated.

New dict tokens RFW_276/277 + RQOS_124, appended in lockstep (6784 lines x 25
packs), English-seeded - they join the RGK_61/RSEC translate pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
